        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d2030aff-5ffb-5175-8f98-2167b3592d0b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: HMS Seraph (P219), Operation Mincemeat\n- Organizations: British intelligence, Royal Marines, Allies\n- People: Glyndwr Michael, William Martin\n- Events: World War II, 1943 Allied invasion of Sicily\n\nFacts:\n- During World War II, HMS Seraph (P219) carried out multiple intelligence and special operations activities.\n- During World War II, HMS Seraph (P219)'s most famous special operation was Operation Mincemeat.\n- In 1943, Operation Mincemeat was a deception intended to cover the Allied invasion of Sicily.\n- In Operation Mincemeat, two members of British intelligence used the body of Glyndwr Michael, a homeless man who died after eating rat poison.\n- In Operation Mincemeat, British intelligence dressed Glyndwr Michael's body as a Royal Marines officer and added personal items identifying him as Captain (Acting Major) William Martin.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
